$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of acid 1 (1.0 g, 3.87 mmol), glycine ester hydrochloride 2
(1.05 g, 4.65 mmol) and DMAP (10 mg, cat.) was dissolved in anhydrous THF
(5ml) and treated with triethylamine (1.58 mL, 11.5 mmol). The reaction
mixture (RM) was then cooled to 0 °C and EDCI.HCl (1.12 g, 5.78 mmol) was
added to it. The resulting solution was allowed to stir at room
temperature for 12 h. After 12 h, the RM was diluted with water (10 ml);
pH adjusted to 7-8 with saturated sodium bicarbonate and the mixture was
extracted with EtOAc (3 × 15 ml). The organic layers were combined, dried
(over Na2SO4) and concentrated under reduced pressure to the residue. The
residue was purified by column chromatography (SiO2, 1:10, Methanol:DCM).
An ester as a colorless liquid (960 mg, 75%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
Chloroform-d) δ 7.82 (ddd, J = 8.6, 2.4, 0.7 Hz, 1H), 7.76 (dd, J = 2.4,
0.7 Hz, 1H), 7.32 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.10-7.03 (m, 2H), 7.00 (d, J =
8.6 Hz, 1H), 6.89 (ddd, J = 8.3, 2.6, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 4.20 (s, 2H), 3.84 (d,
J = 0.8 Hz, 3H), 3.82 (d, J = 0.8 Hz, 3H), 3.77 (d, J = 0.7 Hz, 3H). 13C
NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 170.82, 167.42, 159.25, 159.19, 138.86, 130.40,
129.81, 129.05, 128.32, 125.74, 121.97, 115.21, 112.85, 110.83, 55.73,
55.26, 52.38, 41.56. HRMS (ESI+) m/z: [M + Na+] calcd for C18H19NO5Na
352.1161; found 352.1165.
